            "finding": "Off-by-one: \"`i <= items.length`\" reads \"`items[items.length].quantity`\" and throws a \"`TypeError`\". Every \"`handleOrder`\" call goes through \"`toResponse`\", so it fails after the order has already been saved and the confirmation sent."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "PROPAGATION",
            "severity": "HIGH",
            "location": "src/api.ts:34",
            "finding": "\"`order.total`\" is now in cents (\"`cartTotal`\" returns \"`Cents`\"), but it is still passed to \"`formatEuro`\", which expects euros. A 15 EUR order is shown as \"`1500.00 EUR`\". It should use \"`formatAmount(order.total, order.currency)`\" as \"`handleRefund`\" now does."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "CORRECTNESS",
            "severity": "HIGH",
            "location": "src/order.ts:82-88",
            "finding": "The \"`await`\" was dropped from the async \"`saveOrder(order)`\" call, so a rejection (e.g. \"`order ... already exists`\") is never caught by this \"`try`/`catch`\". Reservations are not released, the confirmation is sent anyway, and the rejection goes unhandled."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "CORRECTNESS",
            "severity": "HIGH",
            "location": "src/order.ts:29,51-52",
            "finding": "\"`options.tags.push(\"bulk\")`\" changes the shared \"`DEFAULT_OPTIONS.tags`\" array (and any options the caller passed in). After one bulk order, every later order created with default options gets the \"`bulk`\" tag, which grows without limit."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "ROBUSTNESS",
            "severity": "HIGH",
            "location": "src/order.ts:54-65",
            "finding": "The duplicate-SKU check runs after all items are reserved and throws without \"`releaseAll(reservedItems)`\", so stock stays reserved for good. The check should come before reserving, or release on failure like the other error paths do."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "PROPAGATION",
            "severity": "MEDIUM",
            "location": "src/refund.ts:21",
            "finding": "\"`refundOrder`\" does not pass \"`order.currency`\" to \"`issueRefund`\", so the \"`\"EUR\"`\" default applies and a CHF order is refunded and reported as EUR."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "DESIGN",
            "severity": "MEDIUM",
            "location": "src/order.ts:21",
            "finding": "\"`customer`\" became optional even though \"`createOrder`\" always requires one. The type is weakened for no reason, and it forces the non-null assertion \"`order.customer!`\" in \"`src/notify.ts:7`\" and a runtime check in \"`validateOrder`\" that this code path can never trigger."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "INTENT",
            "severity": "MEDIUM",
            "location": "src/cart.ts:18-39",
            "finding": "The new exported helpers \"`topItem`\", \"`isValidCart`\" (and \"`describeCode`\" in \"`src/discount.ts:38`\") are not used anywhere. They are speculative scope creep that adds untested surface."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "INTENT",
            "severity": "LOW",
            "location": "src/order.ts:1-91",
            "finding": "The commit message \"`Update order handling`\" does not mention the essential changes: the switch from euros to cents, the new discount kinds and codes, currency support, the minimum order value, and the extra \"`units`\" response field (which changes the API)."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "TESTING",
            "severity": "MEDIUM",
            "location": "src/discount.ts:22-36",
            "finding": "None of the new money logic is tested (cent conversion, percent/seasonal discounts, minimum order value, duplicate-SKU rejection), and the repository has no tests at all. That is how the inverted percent discount and the \"`countUnits`\" crash got through."
        }
    ]
}
